     "text": "Certainly! Based on the latest coding guidelines provided by your mentor, here is a `Heap` class implementation that includes the `insert` and `heapify` methods. The class follows the naming conventions and best practices discussed in our previous sessions, including the use of `y_` as a prefix for variables and the inclusion of `chx` in method names where appropriate.\n\n```python\nclass Heap:\n    def __init__(self, size):\n        self.y_size = size\n        self.y_heap = [0] * (size + 1)  # 1-based indexing\n        self.y_heap[1] = None  # Root node\n        self.y_current_size = 0\n\n    def y_insert(self, value):\n        if self.y_current_size == self.y_size:\n            return False  # Heap is full\n        self.y_current_size += 1\n        self.y_heap[self.y_current_size] = value\n        self.chx_heapify_up()\n\n    def chx_heapify_up(self):\n        current = self.y_current_size\n        while current > 1 and self.y_heap[current] < self.y_heap[current // 2]:\n            self.y_heap[current], self.y_heap[current // 2] = self.y_heap[current // 2], self.y_heap[current]\n            current = current // 2\n\n    def chx_heapify(self):\n        for i in range(self.y_current_size // 2, 0, -1):\n            self.chx_heapify_down(i)\n\n    def chx_heapify_down(self, index):\n        largest = index\n        left = 2 * index\n        right = 2 * index + 1\n\n        if left <= self.y_current_size and self.y_heap[left] > self.y_heap[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right <= self.y_current_size and self.y_heap[right] > self.y_heap[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != index:\n            self.y_heap[index], self.y_heap[largest] = self.y_heap[largest], self.y_heap[index]\n            self.chx_heapify_down(largest)\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **Class Name**: `Heap` \u2013 follows the standard naming convention for a data structure.\n- **Variable Names**: All variables are prefixed with `y_` as per the coding standards.\n- **Method Names**: The `chx_` prefix is used for methods that are specific to the CHEETAH coding standards, as discussed in our",
